url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab14/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunq is a browser-based, noncommercial toy that follows only the
  skeleton of Qix (Taito America, arcade, 1981; Game Boy port published by
  Nintendo, 1990): the player walks the border of an 80x56 field, draws a
  line inward at fast or slow speed, and when the line returns to the border
  the side without the roaming Qix is claimed; slow lines score double.
  Sparks running along the border and the unfinished line are small faces
  of Shushu, a character of the Donghyun series, and a fuse follows a line
  that has stopped. Five modes (basic, villain swarm, twin Qix, fast Qix,
  greedy with a 90 percent target), the starting level (1-9) and the number
  of lives are chosen through a program written in the esoteric programming
  language Donghyun-lang. Input is keyboard and gamepad only, with
  fullscreen; the game is saved in three browser slots and can be exported
  to and imported from a .dhsave file. All graphics, colors and sounds are
  generated by code; no asset of the original games is used or extracted.
  The MIT license applies to the Donghyunq code and documentation; the page
  fonts are under the SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - puzzle game
  - Qix
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
